> Right.  If you are XL 1 when yuou enter minetown, shopkeepers may be
> generated with 11 HD, which brings them *just* in reach of a large dog
> with maxed hit dice. 

A large dog can reach a maximum of ML 9 through kills; since it won't attack
anything two or more levels above it, a ML 11 shopkeeper would still be out
of its reach. Maybe it had found a wraith corpse?

> By default a shk has 12 HD, but there's a downward
> adjustment for sufficiently "over-powerful" monsters.

For being on a shallower DL than the monster's base level. Being of a
lower XL than it doesn't have any effect; the ML can only be increased
for higher player levels. So, unless you're level 16 or higher (the
increment is 0.25 per level difference, rounded down), Minetown
shopkeepers will _always_ be ML 11 (since Minetown can't be deeper
than DL 8).

